# Kconfig — ws component tunables (FW-13; FW-16 server mode).
#
# The device is the WebSocket SERVER (single inbound viewer on
# FIRMWARE_WS_PATH). Three symbols survive:
#
#   FIRMWARE_WS_PATH              — WS endpoint path served by
#                                    esp_http_server on the STA
#                                    interface ("/cams" per PRD
#                                    § FR-5; no MAC substring)
#   FIRMWARE_WS_BUFFER_SIZE       — frame-size sanity bound for
#                                    the greppable parts= log
#                                    metric (16384 default)
#   FIRMWARE_WS_STATUS_PERIOD_MS  — periodic status frame cadence
#                                    (charter L1199: 30000 ms = 30 s)
#
# The outbound-client knobs (URI default, ping/pong, network
# timeout, client task stack) were removed with the client
# lifecycle in FW-16. FW-14 reconnect tunables live in
# main/Kconfig.projbuild (the backoff module is retained but
# unwired in server mode).
#
# Defaults mirrored in firmware/sdkconfig.defaults so the host
# runner's -D cflag mirror picks them up without needing a real
# sdkconfig.

menu "WebSocket Server"

    config FIRMWARE_WS_PATH
        string "WS endpoint path (server mode)"
        default "/cams"
        help
            Path of the WebSocket endpoint registered on the STA
            httpd instance. Must be a literal constant per charter
            L1196 + PRD § FR-5; the identity-leak guard asserts the
            path never contains a MAC substring.

    config FIRMWARE_WS_BUFFER_SIZE
        int "Frame-size sanity bound for stream accounting (bytes)"
        range 1024 65536
        default 16384
        help
            Sanity bound feeding the greppable parts= metric in
            the stream loop log. Frames ride ONE complete binary
            WS message each regardless of this value; it only
            shapes diagnostics.

    config FIRMWARE_WS_STATUS_PERIOD_MS
        int "Periodic status frame period (ms)"
        range 1000 300000
        default 30000
        help
            The status frame fires every N milliseconds while a
            /cams viewer session is active. Disarmed when the
            viewer socket closes. Charter L1199 plus PRD section
            FR-6 set the cadence at 30 s.

endmenu